From 562ac03b6ed852701ad364cd99dde11ccbcbaa6a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 18:33:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 30/32] ehci: start a new isochronous transfer a frame later

A transfer that is not chained to its pipe's previous one started at the
frame after (FRINDEX + threshold) / 8, often the very next frame, which a
controller caching a whole frame had already fetched while the
descriptors were being linked: the first packet never ran. A microphone
reading transfers of four packets on a Toshiba AC100 lost a fifth of its
transactions ("not run" 20 %); one frame more brings that under 0.5 %.

Signed-off-by: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
---
 src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/ehci.cpp | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/ehci.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/ehci.cpp
index 0ea8e31b32..6dc38f230c 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/ehci.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/ehci.cpp
@@ -2135,7 +2135,12 @@ EHCI::SubmitIsochronous(Transfer *transfer)
 			// number in the driver makes no sense for many reason, one of which
 			// is that frame numbers value are host controller specific, and the
 			// driver does not know which host controller is running.
-			currentFrame = ((ReadOpReg(EHCI_FRINDEX) + threshold) / 8)
+			// One frame more than the threshold: the descriptors are
+			// linked after this read, and a controller that caches a whole
+			// frame (IST) had often fetched the first one's frame already,
+			// so its first packet never ran (a fifth of a microphone's
+			// transactions on an AC100, whose transfers are four packets).
+			currentFrame = ((ReadOpReg(EHCI_FRINDEX) + threshold) / 8 + 1)
 				& (EHCI_FRAMELIST_ENTRIES_COUNT - 1);
 		}
 
